{"slug": "clam-or-mussel-stew-with-greens-and-beans", "nyt_id": 1013077, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013077-clam-or-mussel-stew-with-greens-and-beans", "name": "Clam or Mussel Stew With Greens and Beans", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "This is a great winter seafood stew adapted from a much richer recipe by the late Mark Peel, executive chef of Campanile Restaurant in Los Angeles. It’s easy to make and easy to serve.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "½ pound kale, collards or other greens, stemmed and washed in two or three changes of water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "kale", "preparation": "collards or other greens, stemmed and washed in two or three changes of water", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "4 pounds medium-sized clams or mussels (or use a mixture of the two), purged", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "medium-sized clams or mussels", "preparation": "purged", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 large shallot, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large shallot", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 large garlic cloves, sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic cloves", "preparation": "sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "A few sprigs each parsley and thyme", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "a few sprigs each parsley and thyme", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 15-ounce can white beans, drained and rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 16.0, "unit": null, "item": "ounce can white beans", "preparation": "drained and rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 cup chicken stock", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped fresh parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Fill a bowl with ice water. When the water in the pot comes to a boil, salt generously and add the greens. Cook for one to three minutes (depending on the type of green) until just tender. Transfer to the ice water. Allow to cool for a few minutes, then drain, squeeze dry and chop. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Cook the clams or mussels in batches. In a large, lidded pan over medium heat, combine 1 tablespoon of the shallots, one garlic clove, the wine, parsley and thyme sprigs and half the clams or mussels. Bring to a boil, cover and cook about four minutes until they just open. Remove from the pan using tongs, and place in a bowl. Repeat with the remaining clams or mussels. When the seafood is cool enough to handle, remove from the shells, holding the shells over the bowl to catch their juice. Rinse briefly in case there is any lingering sand. Cut the clams in half if they’re large. Strain the liquid in the pan through a cheesecloth-lined strainer into a small bowl, and set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Return the pan to medium heat, and add 1 tablespoon of olive oil. Add the remaining shallots and garlic and salt to taste. Cook gently for three to four minutes until the shallots are tender. Add the remaining tablespoon of olive oil and the chopped blanched greens. Cook, stirring over medium heat, for five minutes. Slowly pour the strained seafood juice into the pan, then add the beans and chicken stock. Bring to a simmer. Simmer five to 10 minutes. The greens should be very tender. Stir in the seafood, add several twists of the pepper mill, taste and adjust salt. Heat through and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 428.8333333333333, "protein_g": 51.3, "carbohydrates_g": 31.9, "fat_g": 8.2, "saturated_fat_g": 1.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.3, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 91.9, "sodium_mg": 2121.0, "fiber_g": 4.4, "sugar_g": 2.1, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course-stew"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["clam", "greens", "weeknight", "white-bean"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/03/10/science/10recipehealth_600a/10recipehealth_600a-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/03/10/science/10recipehealth_600a/10recipehealth_600a-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 81}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-03-10", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:34:54Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "classic-caesar-salad", "nyt_id": 1013104, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013104-classic-caesar-salad", "name": "Classic Caesar Salad", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "There’s a reason clichés like Caesar salad and iceberg with blue cheese dressing have become hyper-common: they’re just good. The combination of cold crunchiness, mild bitterness and salty dressings is everlastingly refreshing and satisfying. This authentic version (get out those anchovies and eggs) from Mark Bittman does not disappoint.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "About ½ cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "about ½ cup extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup rustic bread, cut into 1-inch cubes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "rustic bread", "preparation": "cut into 1-inch cubes", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 clove garlic, halved", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "halved", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 tablespoons freshly squeezed lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "freshly squeezed lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 to 3 tablespoons minced anchovies, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced anchovies", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false, "quantity_max": 3.0}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Dash Worcestershire sauce", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "dash worcestershire sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 large head romaine lettuce, washed, dried and torn into pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large head romaine lettuce", "preparation": "washed, dried and torn into pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup freshly grated Parmesan", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "freshly grated parmesan", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Put 2 tablespoons of the oil in a skillet large enough to hold the bread in a single layer and turn heat to medium. When oil shimmers, add bread and sprinkle with salt and pepper; brown lightly on all sides, adding a little more oil if necessary. Remove and set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Rub the inside of a salad bowl with the garlic clove; discard it. Bring a small pot of water to a boil. Pierce a tiny hole in the broad end of each egg with a pin or needle and boil them for 60 to 90 seconds; they will just begin to firm up. Crack them into the salad bowl, being sure to scoop out the white that clings to the shell."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Beat eggs with a fork. Gradually add lemon juice and 6 tablespoons oil, beating all the while. Stir in anchovies and Worcestershire. Taste and add salt if needed, and lots of pepper. Toss well with lettuce; top with Parmesan and croutons; toss again at table. Serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 423.75, "protein_g": 15.2, "carbohydrates_g": 13.3, "fat_g": 35.5, "saturated_fat_g": 7.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.0, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 99.0, "sodium_mg": 673.5, "fiber_g": 4.8, "sugar_g": 3.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["green-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["anchovy", "easy", "quick", "romaine"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CAESARSALAD1/20COOKING-CAESARSALAD1-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CAESARSALAD1/20COOKING-CAESARSALAD1-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/12/20/dining/20COOKING-CAESARSALAD1/20COOKING-CAESARSALAD1-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 1465}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-04-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:35:00Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "classic-caprese-salad", "nyt_id": 1018849, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1018849-classic-caprese-salad", "name": "Classic Caprese Salad", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "This classic summer dish doesn’t get any simpler or more delicious. Use different-colored heirloom tomatoes for the prettiest salad, and buffalo milk mozzarella for the best tasting one.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "PT15M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound fresh, best-quality mozzarella (preferably buffalo milk)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh", "preparation": "best-quality mozzarella (preferably buffalo milk)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "4 medium heirloom tomatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium heirloom tomatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 bunch fresh basil, leaves only, some reserved for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "bunch", "item": "fresh basil", "preparation": "leaves only, some reserved for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Flaky sea salt, such as Maldon", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "flaky sea salt", "preparation": "such as Maldon", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Coarsely ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarsely ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "High-quality extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "high-quality extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "While mozzarella is cold, slice it into ¼-inch slices. Let it sit, loosely covered, to come to room temperature while you prepare the tomatoes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Slice the tomatoes into ¼-inch to ½-inch thick slices, leaving them in a single layer on the cutting board as you go. Sprinkle generously with salt."}, {"position": 3, "text": "On a serving platter, arrange the mozzarella, tomato slices, and whole basil leaves so they overlap slightly. Pour any tomato juices from the cutting board over the dish. Sprinkle again with salt and pepper, and drizzle with plenty of oil. Top with reserved basil, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 263.8333333333333, "protein_g": 17.8, "carbohydrates_g": 5.5, "fat_g": 19.2, "saturated_fat_g": 10.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.9, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 59.7, "sodium_mg": 392.3, "fiber_g": 1.2, "sugar_g": 2.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer-brunch-lunch-salad-side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["basil", "easy", "five-ingredient", "heirloom-tomato", "mozzarella", "summer", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/07/25/multimedia/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/07/25/multimedia/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/07/25/multimedia/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/07/25/multimedia/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw/MC-Classic-Caprese-fpjw-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 2042}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2017-07-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:21:15Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
